  "2026-10-17T11:41:49.166Z",codex-agent,"The standalone local Bun attempt completed all 666 tests: 660 pass, 5 fail, 1 canceled, 0 skipped/todo. It passes the intended standalone catalog checks and reproduces consumer/startup deadlines, server graph wall time, fatal-output child timing and a reset collaboration connection. Its executable TypeScript/CSS sources match the accepted code head byte for byte. This remains a failed local attempt, separate from the four complete clean-runner npm/Bun gates already green on code head 3eb50e7. Final profile counts, coverage and final tracker-head CI are linked in the public round-3 release receipt. The feature remains in_progress and released; no item was closed."
  "2026-10-18T02:59:46.727Z",codex-agent,"Round 4: collected all seven unresolved review threads and the newest review for 147ba52. Review has no outside-diff or nitpick sections. Verify localization, graph drag/settle/render cost, explicit clears, contrast opacity, and SSE observer selection with independent behavioral revert proofs. Brand main remains 7ad0970d96a20c24b8dbd9e0dcd1efeb8b4d5cc1. Merge current main, run unchanged isolated npm/Bun gates, refresh affected screenshots, push and reply without resolving threads."
  "2026-10-18T03:03:35.458Z",codex-agent,"All seven findings verified. Pinned CLI 2026.10.15 clears description and tags in a real scratch tracker; PATCH now forwards those explicit empties. Real HTTP/PostgreSQL/CLI regression and SSE regression pass 2/2. SSE injects three extra committed-mutation wire facts before content matching. Quick browser passes locale, initial/restarted worker settling, paused drag, cached rendering and nested opacity groups. Twenty steady frames perform zero recolors and zero token property lookups; theme and color mode each invalidate once. Main merged; brand pin remains current."
  "2026-10-18T03:06:49.387Z",codex-agent,Additional issue 218 matches the verified paused-physics drag regression already fixed in handleDragMove. Strengthened round4-drag to use actual Playwright mouse down/move/up on the production canvas. The independent drag revert removes only x/y/velocity assignments; the same real browser gesture must fail. Commit will reference Fixes #218; issue reply follows the push.
  "2026-10-18T03:15:31.431Z",codex-agent,"Round 4 independent behavioral revert proof: nine compiled probes fail as required. Removing only locale binding fails the active accessible name; drag coordinate/velocity assignments fail real mouse displacement; automatic settle fails initial scheduling; worker-fit removal fails initial fit; unconditional recoloring and uncached token values each fail zero steady-frame work; old opacity audit falsely passes faded white ink; dropped empty args fail persisted description/tags; exact SSE count times out after extra wire facts. All unrelated fixes remain current. Production hashes unchanged. Positive matrix passes 42 audits, 778 Tab stops, 255 painted contrast checks, 30 review cases. Real mouse/single-touch retain released positions, cancel pending settling, and preserve pan/click/keyboard behavior for issue 218. The 2000-node/1999-edge worker check returns in 0 ms, completes in 21589 ms, coalesces to one worker, yields input and cancels stale work."
  "2026-10-18T03:17:11.839Z",codex-agent,"Published 18 fixture-only AFTER PNGs for account actions, project graph and item-detail graph at all six width/theme combinations, plus complete unresolved-review input, browser report, nine revert receipts and scale evidence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/tree/pr-screenshots/brand/pm-web-triplicate/round4 . Local strengthened-opacity positive case passes. npm and Bun release checks are running with isolated Git identity, original thresholds and canonical fleet oracle. No threads have been resolved."
  "2026-10-18T03:33:09.834Z",codex-agent,"Final-source rerun passes through pm test: 42 audits, 778 Tab stops, 255 painted contrast checks and 30 review cases in all six width/theme combinations. The initial-fit helper also preserves the first fit after empty data and fits an early hierarchical switch after canceling its worker. The complete nine-case revert script exits 0 after requiring nine independent compiled behavioral failures, with matching production hashes. Build, frontend/server/test type checks, lint, zero duplication and complete docstrings pass. No thresholds or dependencies changed; the held brand main pin is unchanged. Full isolated npm/Bun release attempts remain running and already reproduce tracked catalog/startup, canonical snapshot and server graph-budget failures."
  "2026-10-18T03:42:27.542Z",codex-agent,"Code fixes are committed as 3a061a9560faa0d84ffa1df16b5eeae7f804eb2c, including Fixes #218. Final-source browser acceptance and all nine independent behavioral reverts pass with matching source hashes. A fresh committed-source 2000-node worker run returns in 0 ms and completes in 23309.8 ms, with coalescing, input yielding, static intermediate positions and cancellation all passing. Both isolated local npm/Bun attempts finish with 663 passed, 3 failed, 1 canceled, 0 skipped/todo out of 667; details remain in pm-web-qdhx, pm-web-hqqp and new pm-web-5e1q. These local failed profiles began before the final browser-only refactor and are separate from required final-head CI. Thresholds, scope and deadlines remain unchanged. Final CI receipts and the per-thread replies will be linked in PR 216 and the published round4 evidence directory. Release the claim for orchestrator verification; keep this item in progress."
  "2026-10-18T04:33:43.035Z",codex-agent,"Round 5 started after reading the updated owner contract and synchronizing the PR branch; main is already included. Scope: context-management copy in four locales and static fallbacks, readable graph facets, persistent titled item-sheet header, outlined disabled actions, request-bound failed-edit cleanup, tooltip observer batching, and accessible health warning semantics. Read all unresolved threads and the latest full review body (three inline findings, no outside-diff or nitpick sections). Open issue #218 is already behaviorally fixed in round 4; add its closing keyword to the PR body. Tests will include independent behavioral revert proofs, fixture screenshots at six viewport/theme combinations, and both isolated-identity release gates at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-18T04:47:15.009Z",codex-agent,"Round 5 focused tests passed 16/16 through the pinned pm test runner. The main fixture matrix passed 48 keyboard/contrast audits and captured 36 AFTER screenshots across 1440/768/390 in light and dark. Independent reverts currently reproduce API cleanup, marker ownership, tooltip observer, health warning and facet clipping defects; remaining probes and live-record matrix continue. Decline the suggested canary health-score text: it is 1.68:1 on the light sheet and violates the owner rule reserving canary for working states/copies. Warning scores instead use graphite plus Needs attention, with 49/50/79/80 boundary checks. The contrast harness now skips fully transparent source layers while retaining the existing 3.98:1 partially transparent failure probes."
  "2026-10-18T04:56:36.750Z",codex-agent,"Final round 5 source passes all 10 independent behavioral reverts: API cleanup, same-item marker ownership, observer batching, health bands, facet clipping, titled header, disabled outline, surface parsing, owner copy and transparent-layer contrast. Both grouped runners exit zero and verify production target files remain unchanged. Proofs: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/blob/pr-screenshots/brand/pm-web-triplicate/round5/revert-proofs.json . The final fixture matrix has 72 AFTER images, 138 executed audits, 3032 Tab stops and 851 painted text pairs; 42 live cases pass across six viewport/theme groups. The extended stamp initially wrapped a tablet row; compact author/surface stamps plus a shrinking caption now preserve its geometry, with full tooltip and polite announcement retained. The issue #218 mouse/touch/pending-worker/pan/click/keyboard regression also passes against the final source. Focused tests pass 16/16, including overlap with identical marker expiry timestamps. Zero duplication and frontend type checks pass at unchanged policy. npm release coverage continues after reproducing an existing catalog-consumer failure; no failed run is acceptance."
  "2026-10-18T05:13:09.829Z",codex-agent,"The held kit main advanced to 98cbe45976b3111f09143c2a29ede906cb553c2a during verification. Re-pinned exactly and restarted npm/Bun gates from verified standalone inputs with independent test storage and isolated HOME/global/system Git identity. The kit update changes identity controls only: all 54 consumed assets and the browser palette bundle are byte-identical; a post-pin six-case UI smoke passes. The real HTTP/SSE surface-stamp test passes on the fix and fails when only emitItemEvent is reverted, bringing demonstrated revert proofs to 11. The superseded prior-kit gate attempts were explicitly stopped and are not acceptance. Strict tracker health passes; validation succeeds with existing metadata warnings, which is a separate result."
  "2026-10-18T05:51:19.649Z",codex-agent,"Final pinned local release results are failures: npm 661 passed, 5 failed, 1 canceled; Bun 662 passed, 4 failed, 1 canceled; 667 reported tests each, zero skipped/todo. Statement/line coverage is 91.68% / 91.73%, below the unchanged 92.07% floor. Branch/function results are npm 81.21% / 95.80% and Bun 81.41% / 95.80%. Both scripts stop at coverage, so later stages are not local acceptance. The missing standalone Git metadata suppressed the four identity test declarations; repaired profiles separately pass 4/4 each against trusted main, without changing controls. Catalog/startup evidence is retained in pm-web-qdhx and graph wall-time evidence in pm-web-hqqp. The build-first linked focused suite passes 16/16. All requested copy/layout/review fixes, 72 AFTER screenshots and 11 revert proofs are ready. Push and exact-head CI are the remaining delivery checks. Keep this item in progress for orchestrator verification; no item is closed."
  "2026-10-18T08:40:07.188Z",codex-agent,"Round 6: read all three unresolved threads, latest full review including outside-diff Metadata finding, screenshot review, and open issue #218. Branch contains current main. Plan: single detail title/strip with title-adjacent live slip; count metadata facets; action-specific import/export failures; exact screenshot matrix filter. Add behavioral regression and independent revert proofs, run isolated npm/Bun gates, publish six detail and graph frames plus live-detail frames, verify fresh-clone health and exact-head CI. No thread resolution, merge or release."
  "2026-10-18T08:44:12.722Z",codex-agent,"Round 6 quick browser acceptance passes all four cases: escaped action-specific failures, two/zero metadata facets, one strip/title/caption, and title-owned live slip with stable draft geometry plus reduced motion. Browser discovered intrinsic header resizing; flex fill corrects it. Body-field updates route to the shared detail caption. npm ci initially hit ambient allow-scripts configuration; clean user-config install passes without tracked dependency changes. Current published CLI is 2026.10.18; pinned SDK remains 2026.10.15 as required."
  "2026-10-18T08:48:39.612Z",codex-agent,"Round 6 matrix passes: 24 AFTER frames (detail, graph, live title arrival and settled state; 1440/768/390 x light/dark), 48 accessibility audits, 832 Tab stops, 277 painted text pairs and 24 review cases. Issue #218 real mouse/touch/pan/click/keyboard checks pass in all six groups. Six independent reverts fail: old export/import catch text; duplicate detail strip; live-root suppression (missing title slip); fixed Metadata text; broad PNG selector (34 frames fail expected 30); intrinsic header width (geometry assertion). All production targets remain unchanged by probes. Shared fixture-clock and event helpers restore 0% duplication; explicit child-process result typing passes the complete test TypeScript project. Full isolated npm/Bun gates are restarting on final inputs."
  "2026-10-18T08:53:40.471Z",codex-agent,"Fresh git clone --no-local of 58edb5b passes pinned pm health --strict-exit --require-merge-drivers after clean dependency and pinned managed-extension installation. Authority ok, exit 0; only inherited stale_in_progress_items:17 is advisory. Screenshot branch now publishes the 24 fixture frames and six-revert receipt under brand/pm-web-triplicate/round6. Required npm/Bun release sequence runs on Node 26.12.0 with fresh HOME and disabled global/system Git identity; catalog end-to-end checks remain in progress."
  "2026-10-18T09:04:04.473Z",codex-agent,"Current main advanced to the 2026.10.18 release during gates. Merged it normally as b00bc09 with clean package version reconciliation; review fixes and all visual TypeScript/CSS inputs are unchanged from 58edb5b. The worktree gate had three sibling-fleet catalog mismatches; it was stopped after the base advanced and is incomplete. Final full npm/Bun gates will run in a standalone git clone with the trusted main ref, identical pinned dependencies and CI Git identity isolation. No catalog assertions or thresholds are changed."
  "2026-10-18T09:07:50.951Z",codex-agent,"Catalog boundary reproduced separately on merged inputs: node --test test/catalog.test.ts reports 18 tests, 15 pass, 3 fail, zero canceled/skipped/todo. Failures are inferred fleet membership, Jev description freshness, and snapshot/live metadata equality. Existing follow-ups pm-web-4p94 (partial sibling discovery) and pm-web-5hdb (ADO/Jev metadata drift) own this scope; no duplicate item is needed. Final release evidence uses a standalone clone, retaining the same structural catalog and committed-snapshot assertions used by CI."
  "2026-10-18T09:31:22.755Z",codex-agent,"Round 6 final local acceptance: npm run release:check AND bun run release:check both pass in the standalone merged-head clone (5ed1d5c), Node 26.12.0 with fresh HOME and disabled global/system Git identity. Each: 671/671 suite tests, 2/2 capacity cases, 4/4 real packed consumers; zero failures/cancellations/skips/todos; 40 server files; 92.52% statements/lines, 81.50% branches, 96.12% functions; 0% duplication; 752 documented declarations; zero production vulnerabilities. Six independent revert proofs and 24 AFTER screenshots are published. All 11 reviewed TypeScript/CSS hashes remain identical to the captured implementation. Existing catalog follow-ups remain separate. Final-head fresh-clone health and CI will be maintained in the round6 receipt. Implementation is ready for orchestrator verification; item remains in_progress and is not closed."
  "2026-10-18T09:32:30.587Z",codex-agent,"Required immediate pre-push brand check found new kit main afc46c4352ef429afec38d5bcf04549dd3f1c87d (identity/workflow controls). Reclaiming the item to re-pin, independently compare every consumed asset and canvas palette bundle, and repeat both full release gates. Prior full npm/Bun results remain accepted only for the previous 98cbe45 pin."
  "2026-10-18T09:33:35.747Z",codex-agent,Re-pinned held kit to afc46c4352ef429afec38d5bcf04549dd3f1c87d. All 54 consumed assets and the canvas palette bundle are byte-identical to 98cbe45. Only the exact Git dependency changes; runtime pins remain untouched. Preserved the existing Git-lock format without npm-only archive SRI so npm and Bun retain their established archive compatibility. Refreshing the complete 24-frame matrix on the new pin while repeating both full gates.
  "2026-10-18T09:59:35.684Z",codex-agent,"Current-pin npm repeat observed the known pm-web-qdhx failure: unchanged smoke test 'server entrypoint exits non-zero without DATABASE_URL' exceeded its 10000 ms execFileSync deadline (10179 ms); killed/timed-out child reports no numeric exit code, correctly failing the assertion. Server/startup implementation is unchanged by this review and the kit update is byte-identical. Preserve the full failed attempt, finish both required repeats, and use exact-head CI as separate evidence. No deadline, assertion or threshold is weakened."
  "2026-10-18T10:30:39.531Z",codex-agent,"Final held-kit afc46c4 full repeats are failed attempts: npm 670 passed / 1 failed / 0 canceled; Bun 669 passed / 1 failed / 1 canceled, out of 671 each; zero skipped/todo. npm missing-DATABASE_URL child exceeds the unchanged 10000 ms deadline; focused identical-pin test passes 1/1 at 9802 ms. Bun catalog case exceeds unchanged 300000 ms, then source case reports spawn ENOTDIR. Existing pm-web-qdhx owns these startup/cleanup cases. Later capacity/audit/packed stages are not reached on this pin locally. Prior complete npm/Bun gates on the byte-identical previous kit remain separate historical acceptance, not a green current-pin receipt. All 24 current-pin screenshot frames, 48 keyboard/contrast audits and six behavioral reverts pass. No assertion, source scope, dependency floor or coverage threshold is weakened. Final-head CI/health receipts are linked from the round6 evidence directory. Releasing the item in_progress for orchestrator verification; not closing it."
  "2026-10-18T10:32:49.012Z",codex-agent,"Brand main advanced again before PR push, to 505f386aaa68c0947b9380eae9cfe74dc48e47c7 (package banners and context-management documentation). Re-pin and compare consumed bytes. To validate an immutable candidate before updating the PR branch, run the repository's unchanged CI workflow via workflow_dispatch on a separate validation branch; it executes full npm AND Bun release checks with identity isolation on Node 22/26. Keep current local afc46c4 failed attempts separate. Final immutable-head gate, health and screenshot receipts will be maintained under the round6 evidence directory; no assertion or threshold changes."
  "2026-10-18T10:34:21.314Z",codex-agent,"Latest held kit 505f386 is installed. All 54 consumed asset hashes and the canvas bundle remain identical across 98cbe45, afc46c4 and 505f386. Immutable validation candidate will run the unchanged full CI workflow (npm and Bun on Node 22/26) before the PR branch is updated; no workflow changes, release or deployment. Local afc46c4 outcomes remain npm 670 pass/1 fail and Bun 669 pass/1 fail/1 canceled, with focused startup 1/1, under pm-web-qdhx. Current-pin screenshots are refreshed from fixture data. All final immutable-head gate/health receipts are linked from brand/pm-web-triplicate/round6 on pr-screenshots. Claim released for orchestrator verification; item stays in_progress and is not closed."
